==Trivia==
*[[Version 4.0 Update|Version 4.0]] gave Wheel Cat the [[Massive Damage|massive damage]] to [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] ability.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Solar Cat was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Cool Breeze, Hot Day (Removed Combo)|Cool Breeze, Hot Day]] and [[Sun and Moon (Removed Combo)|Sun and Moon]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Wheel Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Wheel Cat
Got tired of changing wheels of vehicles
so became one instead. Spins so fast it burns.
Massive damage against Aliens (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Solar Cat
Got tired of moving around
so decided to become a galaxy instead.
Massive damage against Aliens (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Chill Cat
An evolved Cat who is always
calm and collected at the office.
Massive area damage to Aliens.</pre>
*Wheel Cat is based on [[wikipedia:Wanyūdō|wanyūdo]], a ''yōkai'' that appears as the head of a tormented man trapped within a burning oxcart wheel. This is why he's included in [[Paranormal Activity (Combo)|Paranormal Activity]].
*In [[The Battle Cats POP!]], Wheel Cat's descriptions mention that it is "powerful vs Aliens". However, not only are there no Aliens in this version of the game, but it does not have Massive damage.
**Wheel Cat also has two spritesheets in the game, with one being [[Media:038 f cut.png|a bugged version that goes unused]].
*Although Chill Cat is blue in The Battle Cats, in [[Nyanko Defence Force]] it appears yellow.

